on help ()
	//Print the REPL slash-command reference.
		//5/7/26 by JES (PR 7)
			//Thin wrapper around the repl.help kernel verb, which calls
			//repl_output_help() in C to emit the legacy slash help text.
			//PR 6 had this print directly via a `stdout` verb that is not
			//defined in headless mode, so PR 7 added the kernel verb and
			//rewrote the handler. The menubar's "Help" item now installs
			//"repl.help ()" directly (see installReplMenubar.ut), so this
			//handler is no longer reached at runtime - it is preserved so
			//a future host can hook UserTalk customization in here.
	repl.help ()
	return (true)